<!-- MODULE 11: WHAT WE CHANGED -->
<section class="cs-interventions" aria-labelledby="interventions-heading">
  <div class="cs-interventions-inner">
    <h2 class="cs-h2" id="interventions-heading">What We Changed and Why</h2>

    <div class="cs-intervention-list">

      <div class="cs-intervention">
        <div class="cs-intervention-num" aria-hidden="true">01</div>
        <div>
          <div class="cs-intervention-title">Gave Branded Demand a Clearer Campaign Responsibility</div>
          <p class="cs-intervention-desc">We separated Brand Search so branded demand could be measured and managed independently from broader product and category searches. This gave the team a clearer view of Brand Search performance and made non-brand performance easier to evaluate during the documented period.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cs-intervention">
        <div class="cs-intervention-num" aria-hidden="true">02</div>
        <div>
          <div class="cs-intervention-title">Separated Non-Brand Search by Intent</div>
          <p class="cs-intervention-desc">Higher-intent product and category searches were separated from broader discovery activity so their performance could be evaluated against more relevant expectations. Campaign structure and bidding settings were then reviewed against the conversion behavior of each group.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cs-intervention">
        <div class="cs-intervention-num" aria-hidden="true">03</div>
        <div>
          <div class="cs-intervention-title">Added Verified Customer Data as Performance Max Audience Signals</div>
          <p class="cs-intervention-desc">We added verified customer purchase data as an audience signal in Performance Max and organized product coverage around clearer campaign responsibilities. Audience signals guide Google's machine learning but do not restrict targeting exclusively to the uploaded list. We also used available brand and query controls to reduce unnecessary overlap with Search where the account setup supported it.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cs-intervention">
        <div class="cs-intervention-num" aria-hidden="true">04</div>
        <div>
          <div class="cs-intervention-title">Introduced a Dedicated Upper-Funnel Test</div>
          <p class="cs-intervention-desc">We launched dedicated Discovery activity to test broader reach and consideration separately from Search and Shopping. Its immediate platform ROAS was below 1&times; during the documented period. Because the campaign served an upper-funnel role, it was evaluated using a broader set of indicators rather than expected to match Brand Search on immediate return.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="cs-intervention">
        <div class="cs-intervention-num" aria-hidden="true">05</div>
        <div>
          <div class="cs-intervention-title">Aligned Campaign Expectations with Campaign Role</div>
          <p class="cs-intervention-desc">Rather than evaluating every campaign against one identical ROAS expectation, we reviewed bidding and measurement in the context of each campaign's role, available conversion volume, and the brand's broader commercial objective.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </div>
</section>

